# tithe6 - the SQUARE face
#
# The same three rows in a CGA cell, but five pixels wide rather than
# three. It exists because of the ASPECT: a CGA pixel is 2.4:1 tall, so
# tithe4's 3x5 ink is READ as 3 wide by 12 tall and tithe6's 5x5 as 5 by
# 12. tools/os88font.py's own header says a face balanced on VGA can be
# spindly there and that is the adapter it will be read on.
#
# 6x6 cell, 5x5 ink - the last column and the last row are the
# ADVANCE, so a run of glyphs never needs a gap put between them.
# Codes 1..7 are the stat ICONS: one glyph set and one renderer, so a
# number and the thing it is a number OF are drawn the same way.
#
# AN ICON IS UP AGAINST THE DIGITS IT SITS BESIDE. At five pixels the
# coin was the digit 0 and the shield was the heart with one row
# changed, so the coin is SOLID where 0 is outlined and the shield is
# OUTLINED where the heart is solid - mass, not detail, is what reads
# at this size. The sword's guard is low for the same reason: a centred
# one is the '+'.
#
# '#' IS BOTH THE INK AND THE COMMENT MARKER, so a reader must test
# for a PIXEL ROW before it tests for a comment - tools/os88font.py
# carries the same warning and this file's reader walked into it.

